{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "ShokoohSaremi2004-Cband-cube-PBS-needle",
  "Source": "M. Shokooh-Saremi, M. Nourian, M. M. Mirsalehi, S. H. Keshmiri, \"Design of multilayer polarizing beam splitters using genetic algorithm,\" Optics Communications 233, 57-65 (2004). doi:10.1016/j.optcom.2004.01.008 - Table 2, column Needle (p. 63); design settings text p. 62",
  "Notes": "C-band cube polarizing beam splitter, designed by the needle method (FilmWizard) for comparison\nSpecification: Same as GA design: C-band cube PBS, 45 deg in n=1.5 glass, Rs -> 1, Rp -> 0 over 1528-1560 nm; needle settings: initial total thickness 6000 nm, max 20 layers, min layer thickness 10 nm, 50 iterations.\nReported: 20 layers; sum d = 7.4081 um; sum(nd) = 12.367 um; P over band: max 1.0, min 0.9930, mean 0.9980, std 0.0016; yield 100 %. Fig. 9: Rp rises to ~1.7 % at 1570 nm.\nNotes: Table order is incident (A) -> substrate (S), kept as is. Angstrom converted to nm. Note the 7th layer is 11997 A (1199.7 nm) as printed. Recomputed sum d and sum nd match the table.\nLayers from Table 2, column Needle (p. 63); design settings text p. 62; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours total 7408.1 nm; P min 0.9930, mean 0.9977; paper total 7408.1 nm; P min 0.993, mean 0.998.",
